<title>CANADA: Canada body details Red Winter Wheat protein.</title>
<headline>Canada body details Red Winter Wheat protein.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Canadian Grain Commission on Monday detailed the protein content of Canada Western Red Winter Wheat.</p>
<p>			   No1 CWRW</p>
<p>PROVINCE	SAMPLES   MEAN AVG  MIN. MAX. (PCT)</p>
<p>Manitoba	   6	11.3     10.0  12.0</p>
<p>Saskatchewan    53	10.6	8.7  13.2</p>
<p>Alberta	  122	11.8	8.8  15.6</p>
<p>W. Canada	181	11.4	8.7  15.6</p>
<p>			   No2 CWRW</p>
<p>PROVINCE	SAMPLES   MEAN AVG  MIN. MAX. (PCT)</p>
<p>Manitoba	   8	10.8	9.5  12.4</p>
<p>Saskatchewan    41	10.4	8.3  13.6</p>
<p>Alberta	   17	10.4	8.3  13.8</p>
<p>W. Canada	 66	10.4	8.3  13.8</p>
<p>			   CW FEED</p>
<p>PROVINCE	SAMPLES   MEAN AVG  MIN. MAX. (PCT)</p>
<p>Manitoba	   7	10.4	9.9  10.9</p>
<p>Saskatchewan    55	 9.5	7.7  12.3</p>
<p>Alberta	    7	 9.7	8.1  12.6</p>
<p>W. Canada	 69	 9.6	7.7  12.6</p>
<p>			   ALL GRADES</p>
<p>PROVINCE	SAMPLES   MEAN AVG  MIN. MAX. (PCT)</p>
<p>Manitoba	  21	10.8	9.5  12.4</p>
<p>Saskatchewan   149	10.1	7.7  13.6</p>
<p>Alberta	  146	11.5	8.1  15.6</p>
<p>W. Canada	316	10.8	7.7  15.6</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548))</p>
